  "notes": "Cash-basis county, FY ending 6/30/2025. Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Beginning cash = fund balances beginning of year (6,624,673, same before and after the Note 10 restatement, which only moves 1,440,797 from the Inheritance Fund to the General Fund). ending_cash 4,328,675 = cash 2,025,243 + investments 95,341 + restricted cash 2,208,091 (p1/p3), the balance the statement rolls forward; investments are inside ending_cash, so ending_investments is left null. Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): taken from the Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Cash Basis, Governmental Funds, Total Governmental Funds column (p3), whose totals (4,328,675) equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); fund balance by classification (restricted, committed, unassigned) replaces the government-wide Unrestricted 2,120,584. Taxes line split using the Statement of Activities (p2): Property 2,172,068, Motor vehicle 144,615, Lodging 10,112, Other 8,656 sum to 2,335,451, $2 more than the 2,335,449 on p4, so property tax is recorded as 2,172,066 (computed) to tie p4; the $2 is in report_discrepancies. Principal and interest 65,555 split using the Nonmajor Total column (p8: principal 45,000, interest 20,555). Local receipts 603,655 mixed category (charges, interest, miscellaneous per p2), recorded as charges for services/fees with review. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p9) is the departmental detail for the General Fund column; p5 combining General Fund page (function-level) not double counted except its Inheritance Tax Fund column (not in the budget schedule). Function split in p9 departments differs from the p5 function lines (e.g. general government 1,355,106 vs 1,346,035) but both total 2,636,403; capital outlay 97,732 is embedded in departments. Road fund and Courthouse Building budget schedules have a single disbursements line (not itemized). Nonmajor combining has 9 funds (p6-8), so only the Total column (p8) is recorded. No business-type funds; no utility schedules. Transfer cross-check: General Fund 1,157 + Inheritance Tax Fund 700,000 = 701,157 out, matches Courthouse Building transfers in 701,157 (p4, p11); nonmajor transfers 10,163 out of 911 Emergency Fund to 911 Wireless Service Fund net to zero within nonmajor funds; total transfers in 711,320 = out 711,320. No transfers hidden in spending lines. Attempt 3 (charges-for-services re-check of the 'Local' lines): statement Local 603,655 and General Fund Local 562,460 stay charges for services/fees, since the Statement of Activities (p2) charges for services 343,799 are 57% of the statement line and at least 54% of the General Fund line (no line-by-line breakdown printed, so no split); Road Fund Local 11,974 moved to other (public works has no charges for services on p2); Courthouse Building Local 26,638 moved to other (unexplained); nonmajor Local 2,583 (entirely the Register of Deeds Preservation & Modernization Fund, p6) moved to Fees of Office. No amounts changed; totals and roll-forward unchanged. Read pages 1-11 of 11",
